# Benchmark frames

The nine frames are the Hugging Face dataset `d-SEAMS/h2h-systems`.
`python3.12 scripts/h2h_fetch.py` downloads each xz dump with
huggingface_hub and unpacks it into `h2h-cpc/systems`. When that
download fails, the script builds the frame with
`scripts/h2h_cpc.py prepare`.

Ice Ic uses a conventional cell of a = 6.358 Å. Liquid and the
interface replicate frame 1 of `input/traj/dump-l.lammpstrj`, scaled by
7/3. The dumps stay out of git. The Snakemake rules `h2h_neighbours`,
`h2h_rings` and `h2h_chill` take the unpacked frames from `h2h_systems`.
